## What is new

- **One build, two addresses:** both frames load the same demo; `?normals=exact` and `?normals=plane` make the
  difference.
- **Controls that name both frames:** `data-demo="#left, #right"` (a CSS selector) on a button or a slider of the
  slide sets both demos at once. The values shown come from the first one.
- **A slider in the slide:** `<input type="range" data-demo-input="ampl">` sets the parameter while it moves, and
  follows its value.
- **Two clocks:** each copy runs its own time. "Restart both" sets them to the same time, so that the two
  ripples stay in phase.

*Rem. Two demos are two WebGL contexts: the browser limits their number in a page (see
[On the day of the talk](../../01_tutorial/10_talk-day/index.html)).*

